{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const defineFieldGroup: DefineFieldGroupFn<Record<never, never>>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts#L255","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts:255"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defines a reusable group of virtual fields that can be bound to concrete\npaths in different parent forms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict"},{"type":"text","value":" when a binding must have exactly the declared value type. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loose"},{"type":"text","value":" when a binding may have the declared type or a narrower assignable\ntype."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const passwordFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  password: strict<string>(),\n  confirmPassword: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface PasswordFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof passwordFieldGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction PasswordFields({ fields }: PasswordFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"password\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"confirmPassword\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const PasswordSection = passwordFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  PasswordFields,\n  'fields',\n)","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst defineFieldGroup: DefineFieldGroupFn<Record<never, never>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts:255](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts#L255)\n\nDefines a reusable group of virtual fields that can be bound to concrete\npaths in different parent forms.\n\nUse `strict` when a binding must have exactly the declared value type. Use\n`loose` when a binding may have the declared type or a narrower assignable\ntype.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nconst passwordFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  password: strict<string>(),\n  confirmPassword: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface PasswordFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof passwordFieldGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction PasswordFields({ fields }: PasswordFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"password\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"confirmPassword\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const PasswordSection = passwordFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  PasswordFields,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: defineFieldGroup\ntitle: defineFieldGroup\n---\n\n```ts\nconst defineFieldGroup: DefineFieldGroupFn<Record<never, never>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts:255](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/FieldGroup/withFields.public.ts#L255)\n\nDefines a reusable group of virtual fields that can be bound to concrete\npaths in different parent forms.\n\nUse `strict` when a binding must have exactly the declared value type. Use\n`loose` when a binding may have the declared type or a narrower assignable\ntype.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nconst passwordFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  password: strict<string>(),\n  confirmPassword: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\ninterface PasswordFieldsProps {\n  fields: typeof passwordFieldGroup.fields\n}\n\nfunction PasswordFields({ fields }: PasswordFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"password\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field name=\"confirmPassword\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            type=\"password\"\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const PasswordSection = passwordFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  PasswordFields,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n"}
